  1	// METHOD-077: one Bayesian CPD registration per call with a chosen Nystroem landmark variant
  2	// (METHOD-076), for the landmark-variant experiment. Not a CTest; driven by
  3	// tools/benchmark/cpd_landmark_variants.py, which owns the run plan, timeouts and merging.
  4	//
  5	//   IntrinsicCoherentPointDriftLandmarkVariants --fixture full|partial --seed S --points N
  6	//       --variant exact|<source>/<schedule>/<pattern> [--landmarks L] [--error-limit E]
  7	//       [--threads T] --out <json> [--positions <bin>] [--reference <bin>] [--dump K]
  8	//
  9	// Fixture: N points on a bumpy closed surface (seeded); truth = similarity(bend(source));
 10	// target = truth + N(0, 0.004^2) noise with every 20th point replaced by uniform clutter;
 11	// "partial" keeps only target points with truth x < 0.2. "exact" runs the exact E-step (Auto)
 12	// and may write its registered points (--positions, only when complete) as the reference other
 13	// variants are compared with (--reference, exactly N positions). Writes one JSON object; exit 0
 14	// complete, 1 incomplete result, 2 usage, 3 no comparison with the reference possible.
